    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d850">

                <pb facs="0891" n="877" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg877"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.5051/7–2744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-03T11:00:00-04:00">August 3, 1944—11
                            a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>956. Address note to Foreign Minister in Uricoechea case, subject of your no.
                    1320, July 27.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d850-f1"/> Ask that he inform the court
                    that immunity should be granted to Rubber Development Corporation, since it is
                    owned and controlled by the Government of the United States, and carries on its
                    activities in Colombia as an agency of this Government, acting under its
                    direction.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
